  "question": {
    "text": "A particle performs simple harmonic motion with amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. Its speed is increased to three times at an instant when its displacement is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. The new amplitude of motion is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is _____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Speed in SHM in terms of displacement is given by, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ω</mi><msqrt><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math>.</p><p>at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ω</mi><msqrt><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi>A</mi><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Let the new amplitude be<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>'</mo></math></p><p>Then, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>v</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>ω</mi><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>'</mo></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi>A</mi><mi>ω</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>A</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>. </p>"
  }
}